  "details": "At the request of VRChat staff member \"pi\" on Discord, I come here with some general feedback to the VRChat team:\n\nI’ve been feeling concerned about the direction some recent VRChat features are taking, particularly around communication and prioritization. When I asked about the reasoning behind the auto-invite/group feature, I didn’t get much clarity, and it made me feel like transparency has decreased compared to before. From my perspective, the feature seems closely tied to retention and engagement goals, and I think it would be helpful if those motivations were communicated more openly when they influence development decisions.\n\nI also feel that automatic group invites don’t always align well with how I and many others naturally use the platform. Most of the time, I’m in public instances because I’m spending time with friends, not because I’m actively looking to join new groups. With the current limitations of group management, additional invites can feel overwhelming rather than helpful. I believe there may be more organic ways to encourage group participation and other areas that could be prioritized first. While I understand that VRChat is a business and needs to be sustainable, and that the developers care deeply about the platform, I hope future decisions can continue to balance business needs with community experience and values.",
